  "note": "Verso body page, no page_header_band at all: this chapter's body pages carry only a yellow footer_rule (#fecb03) with the folio tab, here right-aligned (0.614-1.0). Two columns: a narrow LEFT margin column holding the hanging section headings (5.4.3/5.4.4/5.4.5) and the blue 'Example'/'Solution' labels, and a wide RIGHT column holding all body prose. body_text_size_px=21 measured cap-to-baseline on the 5.4.3 paragraph. The top Example panel (rounded grey frame, white interior, blue #81c4e2 vertical stripe at its left edge) is reported as a `box` frame plus a `decorative_image` for the stripe -- the stripe is NOT a rule_bar (that role is reserved for the chapter-opening divider) and the panel itself has no tint, so giving the box a blue fill would wrongly tint the whole panel. The first 'Solution' label (y 0.124-0.140) matches no A2 block -- A2 bundled the second one into block 4 but left this one out -- so it is n:null, role marginal_note; that role choice is the one genuinely ambiguous call on this page. figure n=2's caption ('cis'/'trans', y 0.2275) and figure n=5's caption ('(a) cis .. (b) trans ..', y 0.4835) are separate figure_caption elements sitting just below each diagram, outside the figure bboxes. 'Reprint 2026-27' at the page foot is recorded as a second running_header."
